To update part of an lO register, without a read-modify-write sequence, the best solution on RP2040 is atomic set/clear/XOR (see Section 2.1.2). Note that this is more flexible than byte or halfword writes, as any combination of fields can be updated in one operation.

Upon a 8-bit or 16-bit write (such as a strb instruction on the Cortex-M0+), an lO register will sample the entire 32-bit write databus. The Cortex-M0+ and DMA on RP2040 will always replicate narrow data across the bus:

