2.15.6.2. Using the frequency counter

To use the frequency counter, the programmer must:

• Set the reference frequency: clk\_ref

• Set the mux position of the source they want to measure. See FC0\_SRC

• Wait for the DONE status bit in FC0\_STATUS to be set

• Read the result

The SDK defines a frequency\_count function which takes the source as an argument and returns the frequency in kHz:

SDK: https://github.com/raspberrypi/pico-sdk/blob/master/src/rp2\_common/hardware\_clocks/clocks.c Lines 245 - 276

